select i.team_id, i.id, $il$Claude$il$, '2026-09-09T10:06:00.000Z'::timestamptz,
$il$Adding Oliver's refinement here rather than as its own nice-to-have item, because the rule has to ship WITH the feature. If it were separate, this item could get built as a must and the refinement skipped as a nice to have, and the result is a subject box on DMs.

WHICH MESSAGE TYPES CARRY A SUBJECT:
  Connection request note  no subject, and blank by default anyway
  DM after CR accepted     NO SUBJECT. Hide the field entirely, do not show it empty
  DM chaser                no subject
  Sales Nav InMail         SUBJECT REQUIRED. Confirm LinkedIn's character cap rather than assuming one
  Cold email, first touch  subject required, new subject
  Email chaser             reuse the thread subject, see below

ON THE EMAIL CHASER, one correction worth having before it gets built. Oliver is right that it should behave like an Outlook follow up, and the prefix is 'Re:'. But the prefix is not what makes it a follow up. Threading is done by the In-Reply-To and References mail headers, not by the subject text. An email that merely copies the old subject and prepends 'Re:' arrives as a NEW conversation in the recipient's client, sitting apart from the original.

So the requirement is: send the chaser as a genuine reply within the existing thread, carrying the original message id. The 'Re:' then comes along for free. Two details that follow: never stack prefixes, one 'Re:' only and never 'Re: Re:', and note that German Outlook renders it 'AW:'. That is only cosmetic since threading is header based, but it is worth knowing when reading a German thread back and wondering why the prefix changed.$il$
