values ((select id from public.teams limit 1), $il$i027$il$, $il$Countries Selling In should be a multi-select, not free text$il$, $il$Lovable UI$il$, $il$Brad$il$, $il$nice$il$, $il$open$il$, $il$Oliver$il$, '2026-09-09T08:55:00.000Z'::timestamptz, 5, '{}'::text[], array[$il$i049$il$]::text[], null, null, false, false, $il${"Oliver": "2026-09-15T13:06:39.809Z"}$il$::jsonb,
$il$Company level. Countries Selling In is a plain text field and needs a picker with multiple selection, restricted to the canonical country list the scoring model already uses. Keep it separate from the single Country field, which is what the legality guard reads. Wiring the multi-select into that guard would make a German company emailable because it also sells into France.$il$,
$il$Oliver marked this nice to have and as UI work it is. But the field is currently unusable as DATA, and two things downstream want to read it:

1. TERRITORY SCORING. Territory is 15 of the 100 points and reads a country name. Free text means a typo, an abbreviation or a German spelling silently scores as 'not in the sequence table, rank 0'. The scoring model already has the canonical list, so the picker should use exactly these values and nothing else:
   Rank 1, 15 pts: Germany, Austria, Switzerland
   Rank 2, 11 pts: France, Spain, Italy
   Rank 3, 7 pts: Netherlands, Belgium, Luxembourg, Ireland
   Rank 0, 3 pts: Poland, Sweden, Denmark, Norway, Finland, Hungary, Czechia, Portugal, Estonia
   Rank -1, 0 pts: United Kingdom (Jack's territory)

2. MULTI-MARKET PROSPECTS ARE A REAL PATTERN, and this is the field that surfaces them. getgoods.com is VAT registered in AT, NL, FR, ES, IT and CH, six markets from one relationship. Otto Austria Group trades in AT, DE and CH. Once this is structured you can filter for partners who span markets, which is a different and better conversation than a single-country attach.

KEEP THE TWO COUNTRY FIELDS DISTINCT. 'Country' is the single home country and is what the legality guard reads, because cold email is permitted for FR, BE, NL and CH-targeted only while DE, AT, ES, LU, IT and CZ are LinkedIn led. 'Countries Selling In' is the multi-select and must not be wired into that guard, or a German company that also sells into France becomes emailable, which it is not.

Same treatment is worth considering for any other field the scoring reads. A picker is not a nicety where a number depends on the string matching.$il$);
