$il$Flagging why this is more than cosmetic, for whoever picks it up. Territory is 15 of the 100 score points and it reads a country NAME. As free text, 'Deutschland', 'DE' or a typo all fall through to 'not in the sequence table, rank 0' and score 3 instead of 15, silently. Nobody sees a wrong score, they see a plausible one. So the picker should emit exactly the strings in the list above and nothing else. The same argument applies to any other field the scoring reads: where a number depends on a string matching, a picker is not a nicety. And keep Country and Countries Selling In apart, because the cold-email legality guard reads Country, and a German company that also sells into France must not become emailable.$il$
