$il$Worth knowing what is hiding in those fields, because it is the evidence that decides the verdict. The Coverage Summary on this record reads 'GREENFIELD (verified 2026-08-05, checkout walked + IPID test + adversarial verify)' and then carries the walked product, the price and the live URL. That is the audit trail behind a greenfield call. If it is clipped to two lines, the one thing a person needs in order to trust or challenge the verdict is the thing they cannot see.$il$
