insert into public.improvements (team_id, item_key, title, category, owner, priority, status, raised_by, created_at, build_wave, blocks, blocked_by, done_by, done_at, pinned, hidden, seen_by, detail, notes)
values ((select id from public.teams limit 1), $il$i029$il$, $il$Research stage goes Outdated on age, and Outdated offers two routes$il$, $il$Research agent$il$, $il$Brad$il$, $il$must$il$, $il$open$il$, $il$Oliver$il$, '2026-09-09T09:15:00.000Z'::timestamptz, 3, array[$il$i003$il$]::text[], array[$il$i001$il$,$il$i041$il$]::text[], null, null, false, false, $il${"Oliver": "2026-09-09T11:17:48.570Z"}$il$::jsonb,
$il$A company whose research is older than three months moves to Research Stage = Outdated. Clicking Outdated offers two routes: queue it into the next automated research batch, or update manually. Outdated is DERIVED from the research date, never a status someone sets, and it must not reduce the score, only lower confidence and flag the row. Align the three month threshold with the two staleness constants already in lead_score.py rather than inventing a third.$il$,
$il$WHY IT MATTERS, with evidence from this batch. Research decays and the decay is not theoretical. ElectronicShop24 has switched insurance carrier TWICE, AmTrust and Generali before 2016, then Allianz Global Assistance 2016 to 2017, now Ostangler. DiTech.at was recorded as self-funded greenfield and turned out to carry a Wertgarantie policy. electronova-luzern.ch was researched off Internet Archive captures up to fourteen months old. A greenfield verdict has a shelf life, and right now nothing expires.

ALIGN THE THRESHOLD, DO NOT INVENT A THIRD ONE. There are already two staleness constants in lead_score.py:
  LEAD_STALE_DAYS  = 90   three months, contacts
  WEDGE_STALE_DAYS = 180  six months, the checkout walk

The code comment on the 180 is worth reading before setting this: 'TP's own procedure says findings go stale at roughly three months; six is used here because retail checkouts change more slowly than ticketing, and it is a choice worth arguing with rather than a fact.' So Oliver's three months matches the contact constant but is half the walk constant. Pick one number for company research and make all three consistent, or say explicitly why they differ. Three defensible definitions of stale is two too many.

SUGGESTED SHAPE:
1. Outdated is DERIVED from the research date, not a status someone sets. It cannot drift out of sync that way.
2. Outdated does NOT reduce the score. The scoring rule is that unassessed is removed from the denominator, never scored zero, and stale evidence should behave the same way: it lowers CONFIDENCE and flags the row, it does not silently demote the company. The wedge component already does exactly this, discounting a stale walk by 4 points and saying so in the reason string.
3. The queue needs a reason on it, 'outdated, last researched 14 Mar', so the agent knows what it is re-checking rather than starting from scratch.
4. Order the batch by what it unblocks. A company with contacts already sourced and outreach sitting in the refused queue is worth re-researching before one with no contacts. Same ordering principle as the refused queue itself.
5. Re-research should DIFF, not overwrite. If the insurance state has changed since last time, that is the single most valuable output and it should be surfaced, not quietly written over the old value.

SAME PLUMBING AS ITEM i025. The comments and instructions field routable to research needs an identical queue with a reason attached. Build one queue that takes jobs from both sources rather than two.$il$);
insert into public.improvement_comments (team_id, improvement_id, who, at, text)
select i.team_id, i.id, $il$Claude$il$, '2026-09-09T09:16:00.000Z'::timestamptz,
$il$One thing to decide before building: does a company go Outdated on the date of the last research run, or on the date of the last CHECKOUT WALK? They are different and the walk is the one that decays meaningfully. Of eight checkouts Oliver walked on 4 September, two overturned a confident desk verdict, both in the optimistic direction. Desk research ageing matters less than an unverified or long-ago walk. If only one date can drive the status, use the walk date.$il$
