values ((select id from public.teams limit 1), $il$i030$il$, $il$Sending a message must move the status to Contacted automatically$il$, $il$Guards$il$, $il$Brad$il$, $il$must$il$, $il$done$il$, $il$Oliver$il$, '2026-09-09T09:30:00.000Z'::timestamptz, 2, array[$il$i003$il$]::text[], array[$il$i005$il$]::text[], $il$Brad$il$, '2026-09-14T18:43:36.619Z'::timestamptz, false, false, $il${}$il$::jsonb,
$il$When a message goes out, Opportunity Status moves to Contacted without anyone setting it, derived from the touch history rather than typed. This is a fix as well as a feature: ten companies with touches on record still read Untouched, including Currys, Samsung and Carphone Warehouse. Three rules must ship with it. Forward only, never demote. Out of Scope flags a contradiction rather than flipping. A company becomes Contacted when any of its contacts has an outbound touch, and that does not cross group boundaries.$il$,
$il$IT IS ALREADY WRONG IN THE IMPORTED DATA, so this is a fix as well as a feature. 195 companies in the lake have at least one touch on record. TEN of them still sit below Contacted, all reading Untouched: Carphone Warehouse C223, Currys C229, Samsung C263, iStore C241, Fairphone C067, Magenta Telekom Austria C312, Drei C313, HoT C328, Congstar C330, haym.infotec C432. Those are not small names. Any worklist that filters on Untouched is offering them up as fresh.

DERIVE IT, DO NOT SET IT. Same principle as the Outdated status in item i029: if a touch record exists, the system already knows, so a human should not be maintaining it. Status should be computed from the touch history rather than typed.

THREE RULES THAT MUST GO WITH IT, or the automation causes damage:

1. FORWARD ONLY, NEVER DEMOTE. The ladder runs (none), To Review, Prospect, Contacted, Active Lead, Partner. A send advances a company to Contacted ONLY if it currently sits below Contacted. Sending a message to an Active Lead or a Partner must never knock it back down to Contacted. This is the obvious way to break it.

2. OUT OF SCOPE IS STICKY AND MUST FLAG, NOT FLIP. If a company is marked Out of Scope and a message goes out, do not quietly set it to Contacted. That hides a contradiction that someone needs to look at, either the send was a mistake or the Out of Scope call was. Raise it instead.

3. COMPANY STATUS DERIVES FROM ITS CONTACTS. A message goes to a person. The company becomes Contacted when ANY contact at that company has an outbound touch. Note this does not cross group boundaries: contacting getgoods does not mark Conrad as contacted, which is correct, and it is why the group level duplicate guard in item i004 is a separate control rather than something this rule can cover.

WORTH DOING AT THE SAME TIME: a one off reconciliation pass over the imported data, so the ten above and anything similar get corrected on the way in rather than being fixed one at a time later.$il$);
insert into public.improvement_comments (team_id, improvement_id, who, at, text)
select i.team_id, i.id, $il$Claude$il$, '2026-09-09T09:31:00.000Z'::timestamptz,
$il$A theme worth naming, because three of the last four items are the same shape. Outdated research (i029), Contacted status (i030) and next_step replacing P0/P1/P3 (i003) are all cases where a human is asked to maintain a value the system can already work out from its own records. Every one of them drifts, and the drift is invisible because a stale value looks exactly like a correct one. The general rule for the build: if it can be derived, derive it, and make the derived value read only in the UI so nobody can set it by hand and desynchronise it.$il$
