$il$Extending this item rather than raising a new one, since it is the same control on a second surface and it shares the dependency on i031.

SO THE FULL ASK IS: a jump button next to the lead name on the OUTREACH card, and a jump button on each URL in the LEAD view, one for the plain LinkedIn profile and one for Sales Nav. Same on the company, opening the Sales Nav account page.

THE LEAD VIEW SCREENSHOT IS DIRECT EVIDENCE FOR i031. Christiaan de Groot's contact record shows a single field labelled LINKEDIN holding https://www.linkedin.com/in/christiaan-de-groot-a23613153, which is the /in/ profile. There is no Sales Nav field on that view at all. Catherine Meng, by contrast, has a Sales Nav URL and no /in/ URL. So the one field is holding whichever of the two happens to exist, which is exactly the collapse described in i031. Two labelled fields, two buttons, is the fix for both items at once.

SMALLER POINT ON THE SAME SCREEN: the URL is rendered as plain selectable text rather than a link. Even before any button exists, a URL field should be clickable.$il$
