insert into public.improvements (team_id, item_key, title, category, owner, priority, status, raised_by, created_at, build_wave, blocks, blocked_by, done_by, done_at, pinned, hidden, seen_by, detail, notes)
values ((select id from public.teams limit 1), $il$i033$il$, $il$LinkedIn URLs are wrong in the record, and there is no trusted source for them$il$, $il$Data & schema$il$, $il$Both$il$, $il$must$il$, $il$open$il$, $il$Oliver$il$, '2026-09-09T10:44:55.000Z'::timestamptz, 1, '{}'::text[], array[$il$i031$il$]::text[], null, null, false, false, $il${}$il$::jsonb,
$il$The LinkedIn URL held for Mirco Krebs does not resolve, and there is no trusted source for these anywhere. Oliver runs the full LinkedIn data export and hands Brad the archive; Brad loads Connections and Invitations into the contact records, writing the URL as LinkedIn itself holds it. This has to come after i031 has split the two URL fields, or the load overwrites the wrong column. Flag mismatches rather than silently correcting them, and validate a URL on save.$il$,
$il$Oliver can export his full LinkedIn data, which gives Connections, Invitations sent and received, and Messages, each carrying the profile identifier as LinkedIn itself holds it. That export is the trusted source, and it should be loaded rather than trusted to typing.

What we need from this:
1. Oliver runs the LinkedIn data export and hands Brad the archive.
2. Brad loads Connections and Invitations into the contact records, writing the URL from the export and never overwriting a Sales Nav URL with it. This depends on i031 having split the two fields first, otherwise the load overwrites the wrong column.
3. Every contact whose URL did not match the export gets flagged, not silently corrected, so we can see how big the problem was.
4. A URL should be validated on save. A profile URL that does not resolve is a data defect, and the record should say so rather than look fine.

Open question for Brad: whether Phantombuster can keep this current on a schedule, or whether the export stays a periodic manual load. Worth knowing before we build around it.

Note on the export, so nobody expects too much of it: it carries DMs only. InMails are not in it and never will be, so it fixes URLs and connection state but it cannot repair the missing message history in i031.$il$);

